meta {
  name: 47 Order Overview (In-House Order ID)
  type: http
  seq: 47
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/order/{{orderId}}/overview
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("returns the order, the notes anchor and the tests", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    expect(d).to.have.property("orderCode");
    expect(d).to.have.property("orderCancelled");
    expect(d).to.have.property("notesReportId");
    expect(d.tests).to.be.an("array");
  });
  test("each test carries the list row, its report and its holder", function () {
    const t = res.getBody().data.tests[0];
    if (t) {
      ["sample", "testName", "department", "report", "holder"].forEach((k) =>
        expect(t).to.have.property(k)
      );
    }
  });
}

docs {
  The read-only **Order Overview** opened from the Order ID of the In-House list. It describes the order
  as THIS branch sees it and changes nothing.

  - `tests` — exactly the rows the In-House list shows for the order: the active branch's samples of
    that order, not deleted, and only the departments the caller may see (the same visibility rule as the
    list, so the two cannot disagree). Each entry:
    - `sample` — the list row itself (`status`, `transfers[0]`, `itemRemoved`, `tatStatus`, ...), so the
      status text ("Sent – Rejected", ...) is computed from the same data as the list.
    - `testName`, `department` (null when none assigned).
    - `report` — the test's report `{ id, status, heldHere, heldAtBranchName }`, `status` one of the nine
      report statuses; `null` until a report exists (it is made at the first Accept). A panel member's
      sample gets its own member report. `heldHere` is true when this branch holds the report.
    - `holder` — only for a sample this branch sent on that has an accepted copy elsewhere:
      `{ branchId, branchName, status }` = the last branch in the chain of copies and the copy's status there
      ("Currently at Branch B: Accepted"). `sample.status` stays this branch's own status.
  - `notesReportId` — the report notes are read and written through
    (`GET/POST /lab-reports/:id/notes`): the first report of the order held at this branch. `null` when this
    branch holds none (nothing accepted here yet, or every test sent away): notes are then not available.
  - `orderCancelled` — a cancelled order is frozen; no notes can be added.

  404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` when the order does not exist in the tenant. An order with no sample at this branch
  returns an empty `tests` list.
